<!--
  Device manifest for the HALs this project supplies to the Redroid 15 image.

  Both entries below are AIDL, and both are load-bearing for the same reason:
  frameworks/base/libs/vibratorservice and the sensor service stack ask
  AServiceManager_isDeclared() first and only fall back to the HIDL client --
  which waits forever when no HIDL service is registered -- when the AIDL HAL is
  not declared:

    connectHal (libvibratorservice.so @0x11680):
      isDeclared("<IVibrator>/default") == false
        -> V1_0::IVibrator::getService("default")  => "Waited one second ..."
           forever, and the 65 s Watchdog kills system_server (round 69).

  The service implementations live in vendor/native/HostDevicesA15.cpp and are
  launched by the host as the "host-devices" program.

  android.hardware.vibrator  AIDL version 2, IVibrator + IVibratorManager.
  android.hardware.sensors   AIDL version 2, ISensors (empty sensor list; the
    image's system/bin/sensorservice is launched by the host and registers the
    "sensorservice" binder name that DeviceStateManagerService waits for).

  android.hardware.thermal   AIDL version 3, IThermal. HardwarePropertiesManager
    Service's JNI (getThermalHalLocked) asks isDeclared() first and falls back
    to the HIDL 1.0 client, which waits forever because the image only declares
    and ships thermal 2.0. This entry plus the NoThermal service is what lets
    StartHardwarePropertiesManagerService return. Version 3 is the current AIDL
    interface version in android-15.0.0_r36 (hardware/interfaces/thermal/aidl).

  Version numbers come from the image libraries themselves
  (BnVibrator/BnSensors::getInterfaceVersion both return 2).
-->
<manifest version="1.0" type="device">
    <hal format="aidl">
        <name>android.hardware.vibrator</name>
        <version>2</version>
        <fqname>IVibrator/default</fqname>
        <fqname>IVibratorManager/default</fqname>
    </hal>
    <hal format="aidl">
        <name>android.hardware.sensors</name>
        <version>2</version>
        <fqname>ISensors/default</fqname>
    </hal>
    <hal format="aidl">
        <name>android.hardware.thermal</name>
        <version>3</version>
        <fqname>IThermal/default</fqname>
    </hal>
</manifest>
